    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "A seed is like a tiny lunchbox. Inside are a baby plant and food to help it grow.",
      "punch": "lunchbox",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌰",
        "text": "Inside a seed",
        "cue": "lunchbox",
        "sub": "Baby plant + food",
        "sub_cue": "baby"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What does it need to wake up?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Water, warmth and air! In damp, warm soil, the seed soaks up water and splits open.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "A seed needs",
        "icon": "🌰",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "text": "Water",
            "cue": "water",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "☀️",
            "text": "Warmth",
            "cue": "warmth",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "icon": "💨",
            "text": "Air",
            "cue": "air",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then does a leaf pop out?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "First a root grows down to drink water. Then a little shoot pushes up toward the light.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "Sprouting",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "label": "A root grows down",
            "cue": "root"
